# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plans 00194 and 00203 (M0, M1, M2, the board, the health check and timer state fixes):
# rebuilds ccy 3.99.4, ccy-teams and the ccy image (container 2.71; the first launch after it
# rebuilds the image once). The team watcher
# survives a homeserver restart and runs supervised. Every ccy session started in ccy's tmux
# carries the agent team bus kit, idle on no team (no hooks run, its own status line, no inbox
# socket), with its membership mounted read-only; `ccy --no-bus` leaves the kit out. Each
# session's seats are held by one seat keeper process, so a stray background process can no
# longer keep a seat. The ccy-teams board shows each team's health problems on its row.
# Running sessions are unaffected until they are relaunched: relaunch every team session after.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00203 server robustness: each team's homeserver gets readiness and a 30 s watchdog, is
# restarted after any exit but a deliberate stop, and gets a minutely health check (client API
# probe, restart count, backup age). Every live homeserver is backed up, then restarted once on
# the new unit, before the acceptance below has proved that unit here. The play stops at the
# first homeserver that does not report ready within its start timeout (the unit is Type=notify,
# so the start waits for it), naming the team, and leaves the others as they were. Also: the
# kit's pingbus as above (the seat keeper, `seat retire`, `reach`) for `cc --teams` and LXC
# members, seat check waits for a starting homeserver, `agent-bus health status`, and a
# supervised unit for any LXC member entry with service: true. The health check asks each unit
# only for properties its type has (before the fix every run failed with exit 78), and the play
# clears failed health check runs from systemctl --failed, including the removed acc-robust
# team's. Removing a team now clears its backup timer's last-run time (Persistent=true), the
# health check ignores a backup run from before the team's applied stamp, and the play clears
# the last-run time of every agent-bus timer whose team is not installed, so a team made again
# under an old name does not inherit one. No firewall rule changes.
playbooks/imports/play-agent-bus.yml
# Plan 00203 acceptance, every milestone in turn. M2: two throwaway headless ccy sessions in
# ccy's tmux in this checkout (plain and --no-bus, idle, no turn sent), removed after; checks
# the read-only mount, the inert kit, no inbound on no team, idle CPU, the image version and
# --no-bus, on an Enforcing host. Needs ccy launched interactively here once (Quick Launch).
# M1: the helper tests, then a third throwaway plain session: the seat keeper is its only
# pingbus process and only lock holder. Then the server robustness checks (ACCEPTANCE.md
# R1-R9), on a throwaway team acc-robust it removes: kills, ends and freezes its homeserver and
# times its return, shows a stale backup on the board, times seat check waiting for a starting
# homeserver, checks any LXC member unit; its teardown also clears acc-robust's units from
# systemctl --failed and its backup timer's last-run time.
00203-teams-hot-control-and-robustness
# Plan 00201 M7 acceptance again, ported to the M2 launcher (seated sessions found by their
# membership, not the retired ccy-seats label): two throwaway teams, ccy --teams on both, then
# all removed. This is M2's check (a) that ccy --teams works as before, and with M1 that the
# keeper takes the seats.
00201-ccy-teams-many-teams-per-session-descriptions-and-a-picker/acceptance.bash
# Plan 00161 acceptance again, ported the same way (U20's seated headless sessions): its own
# throwaway team, removed after. Also M2's check (a).
00161-agent-team-bus-matrix/acceptance.bash
